# DelayPilot static-asset response headers.
#
# Why this file exists as well as the middleware in apps/edge/src/index.ts:
# wrangler.jsonc sets `run_worker_first` to a list of dynamic prefixes only
# ("/api/*", "/auth/*", "/webhooks/*", "/go/*"), so Cloudflare serves every HTML page
# straight from the edge asset cache WITHOUT invoking the Worker. Verified locally with a
# marker header: GET / and GET /index.html never reach Worker middleware, while
# GET /api/* and unmatched paths do. A Worker-only header policy would therefore have
# left every real page — the ones that actually render HTML — with no CSP and no
# clickjacking protection.
#
# Cloudflare parses this file rather than serving it; it never appears as a public asset.
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# Owner note: apps/web/public/** is seo-engineer territory in docs/agents/ROSTER.md §3.
# This file is a pre-Phase-11 security baseline added under direct owner instruction after
# an external audit; the Phase 11/12 owners should fold it into their wider work rather
# than treat it as settled.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# CSP notes, so the next person does not loosen this by guesswork:
#
# - script-src 'self' — NO 'unsafe-inline' and no hash sources. Every script this build emits is
#   an EXTERNAL same-origin file: /theme-init.js (an endpoint, blocking, pre-paint) and the three
#   bundled `<script type="module" src="/_astro/...">` chunks Astro emits for the header, the theme
#   control and the lookup form. That is a property of the build, not an accident of size:
#   apps/web/astro.config.mjs pins vite.build.assetsInlineLimit to 0, which is what stops Astro
#   inlining a small script chunk into the HTML. Raise it and those scripts become inline elements
#   this policy refuses, so the menus stop opening on the deployed site and nowhere else.
# - Analytics origins (owner-approved). GA4: script-src https://www.googletagmanager.com (the
#   gtag.js loader; its bootstrap is the same-origin /ga4.js endpoint, never an inline script),
#   connect-src https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com
#   https://*.googletagmanager.com and img-src https://*.google-analytics.com
#   https://*.googletagmanager.com (collection hits). Cloudflare Web Analytics: script-src
#   https://static.cloudflareinsights.com and connect-src https://cloudflareinsights.com.
#   scripts/validate-security-headers.mjs pins this exact list; nothing else is third-party.
# - style-src 'self' — NO 'unsafe-inline'. This is earned, not assumed: apps/web/astro.config.mjs
#   pins build.inlineStylesheets to 'never', so the build cannot emit an inline <style>, and the
#   built HTML is verified to contain none. If that setting ever returns to 'auto', every page
#   renders unstyled until 'unsafe-inline' comes back here AND in apps/edge/src/index.ts.
# - img-src 'self' — no `data:`. It carried `data:` only for the placeholder favicon link
#   (<link rel="icon" href="data:,">) that BaseLayout used before an icon set existed. BaseLayout v2
#   now links the real /icons/* files (scripts/assets/asset-manifest.mjs) and the placeholder is
#   gone, and assetsInlineLimit: 0 additionally stops Vite emitting any small asset as a `data:`
#   URI. Nothing in apps/web/dist requests a data: image, so the source was removed rather than
#   left carried defensively. Restoring it would need a real asset that requires it and the same
#   edit in apps/edge/src/index.ts.
# - No frame-src / media-src / worker-src is listed: default-src 'self' already covers
#   them, and enumerating directives the site does not use invites drift.
#
# HOW TO CHANGE THIS POLICY WITHOUT GUESSING. apps/web/scripts/verify-dist.mjs runs on every build,
# refuses any inline <script>, inline <style> or style="..." attribute, and prints the exact
# 'sha256-...' source the header would have to carry for the element it found. So a future inline
# element fails the build with its own allowlist entry already computed: the policy is widened by
# pasting a hash that was measured, or not at all. A `data:` or 'unsafe-inline' source added to
# unblock a red build is the failure mode both this comment and that script exist to prevent.
#
# Whatever changes here must change identically in the SECURITY_HEADERS object of
# apps/edge/src/index.ts: static pages never invoke the Worker and Worker responses never see this
# file, so the same policy is written twice. node scripts/validate-security-headers.mjs compares
# them and fails on any drift.
